# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere.
# This crate is Linux-first and is consumed as a submodule inside a devcontainer
# where a global core.autocrlf=true would otherwise materialize CRLF in the
# working tree on checkout. eol=lf overrides autocrlf so every checkout gets LF
# regardless of the developer's git config, keeping rustfmt output stable and
# the parent workspace's `cargo fmt --all --check` gate green across machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF (explicit belt-and-suspenders).
*.sh text eol=lf
